00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:05,240
which of course is years after the movie.

302
00:12:05,240 --> 00:12:08,920
Any case, so named after John Nash, right?

303
00:12:08,920 --> 00:12:11,000
So instead of player strategies

304
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:16,000
is a pure strategy Nash equilibrium abbreviated PSNE.

305
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:19,640
This is one of the acronyms you must learn for this class.

306
00:12:19,640 --> 00:12:21,000
All right, not many, but this is one of them.

307
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:24,440
PSNE, pure strategy Nash equilibrium.

308
00:12:24,440 --> 00:12:27,120
All right, so if you set up player strategies,

309
00:12:27,120 --> 00:12:28,920
a pure strategy Nash equilibrium,

310
00:12:28,920 --> 00:12:30,960
if no player could do strictly better

311
00:12:30,960 --> 00:12:32,440
by changing strategies,

312
00:12:32,440 --> 00:12:35,200
holding all other player strategies fixed.

313
00:12:36,360 --> 00:12:39,080
Okay, so what does that mean?

314
00:12:39,080 --> 00:12:42,160
Well, imagine asking all the players one by one

315
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:45,240
if they would like to do something different.

316
00:12:45,240 --> 00:12:47,680
If all of them answer no,

317
00:12:47,680 --> 00:12:49,600
then you have a pure strategy Nash equilibrium.

318
00:12:49,600 --> 00:12:50,760
Like what do you mean do something different?

319
00:12:50,760 --> 00:12:53,640
Do something different given what everybody else is doing.

320
00:12:53,640 --> 00:12:55,320
So for example, here's how we test

321
00:12:55,320 --> 00:12:57,240
for pure strategy Nash equilibrium

322
00:12:57,240 --> 00:12:59,440
in the seating arrangement of this room.

323
00:12:59,440 --> 00:13:01,440
So I go to you, given where everyone else is seating,

324
00:13:01,440 --> 00:13:02,920
sitting, do you want to change your seat?

325
00:13:02,920 --> 00:13:03,760
No.

326
00:13:03,760 --> 00:13:04,960
No, given where everyone else is sitting,

327
00:13:04,960 --> 00:13:06,800
including the first two, do you want to change your seat?

328
00:13:06,800 --> 00:13:08,320
No, given where everyone else is sitting,

329
00:13:08,320 --> 00:13:09,600
including the first two people at your desk,

330
00:13:09,600 --> 00:13:10,440
do you want to change your seat?

331
00:13:10,440 --> 00:13:11,280
No.

332
00:13:11,280 --> 00:13:12,760
I go through the entire room.

333
00:13:12,760 --> 00:13:14,280
If 100% of the people say no,

334
00:13:14,280 --> 00:13:15,360
I do not want to change my seat,

335
00:13:15,360 --> 00:13:17,160
given where everybody else is,

336
00:13:17,160 --> 00:13:19,400
we've got pure strategy Nash equilibrium.

337
00:13:19,400 --> 00:13:22,320
If one student says yes, I would.

338
00:13:22,320 --> 00:13:25,360
We don't have a pure strategy Nash equilibrium.

339
00:13:25,360 --> 00:13:26,880
But again, it's not that I would like

340
00:13:26,880 --> 00:13:28,240
to trade seats with that student

341
00:13:28,240 --> 00:13:29,280
because that student is in the seat.

342
00:13:29,280 --> 00:13:30,480
It would have to be like,

343
00:13:30,480 --> 00:13:33,840
you don't want to go and evict them from the seat.

344
00:13:33,840 --> 00:13:36,800
It's got to be that given what they're doing,

345
00:13:36,800 --> 00:13:38,440
you actually want to do something differently,

346
00:13:38,440 --> 00:13:39,280
which could be saying,

347
00:13:39,280 --> 00:13:41,880
would you mind changing seats with me, sir?

348
00:13:41,880 --> 00:13:44,240
Which if you have back trouble, you should try this.

349
00:13:44,240 --> 00:13:48,840
In general, I found that when you plead a medical excuse,

350
00:13:48,840 --> 00:13:50,360
people usually switch seats with you.

351
00:13:50,360 --> 00:13:52,520
So there's no need to be suffering

352
00:13:52,520 --> 00:13:54,720
if you see a better chair around.

353
00:13:54,720 --> 00:13:57,080
It's unusual for someone to say no.

354
00:13:57,080 --> 00:13:59,480
So anyway, some practical advice for this.

355
00:13:59,480 --> 00:14:01,800
But don't be intimidated by what appears

356
00:14:01,800 --> 00:14:03,960
to be pure strategy Nash equilibrium.

357
00:14:03,960 --> 00:14:06,440
Maybe you actually could improve your situation.

358
00:14:06,440 --> 00:14:07,920
If you have back pain,

359
00:14:07,920 --> 00:14:10,480
that's one of the worst kinds of pain in the world.

360
00:14:10,480 --> 00:14:12,480
That's the kind of pain that if you have it,

361
00:14:12,480 --> 00:14:15,120
you don't not have it at any point in your day,

362
00:14:15,120 --> 00:14:16,680
you are feeling pain the entire time.

363
00:14:16,680 --> 00:14:18,400
In my experience with back pain,

364
00:14:18,400 --> 00:14:19,640
unfortunately I don't have it now.

365
00:14:19,640 --> 00:14:22,360
So it sounds a little bit to me that PSNE

366
00:14:22,360 --> 00:14:26,200
is kind of like Pareto efficiency where...

367
00:14:27,600 --> 00:14:28,440
Oh, let's see.

368
00:14:28,440 --> 00:14:30,040
You get no, so no, again, like I said,

369
00:14:30,040 --> 00:14:31,520
it's, let's see.

370
00:14:31,520 --> 00:14:36,200
So I guess you could say that there's no room

371
00:14:36,200 --> 00:14:39,320
for a unilateral Pareto improvement is a way of putting it.

372
00:14:39,320 --> 00:14:42,440
So there's no way for any one person to be better off

373
00:14:42,440 --> 00:14:45,240
holding constant when everybody else is doing it.

374
00:14:45,240 --> 00:14:46,600
Right?

375
00:14:46,600 --> 00:14:49,640
But so I guess there is some similarity,

376
00:14:49,640 --> 00:14:52,120
but again, it's not thinking about like,

377
00:14:52,120 --> 00:14:53,520
you know, like in, like, you know,

378
00:14:53,520 --> 00:14:56,800
but it's still logically possible that say,

379
00:14:56,800 --> 00:14:57,720
there could be a Pareto improvement

380
00:14:57,720 --> 00:15:00,160
by like moving everybody one seat to left, for example,

381
00:15:00,160 --> 00:15:02,000
or make everyone move closer.

382
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:03,960
So that is, that could still be Pareto improvement

383
00:15:03,960 --> 00:15:05,440
even though no one person has to do it.

384
00:15:05,440 --> 00:15:06,520
So I actually take it back.

385
00:15:06,520 --> 00:15:07,680
There's actually no connection.

386
00:15:07,680 --> 00:15:08,560
They're unrelated.

387
00:15:08,560 --> 00:15:09,560
Okay, I get it.

388
00:15:09,560 --> 00:15:10,400
Thank you.

389
00:15:10,400 --> 00:15:11,240
Sure, sure.

